-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  pl_mpeg.pcpp - the pl_mpeg unit (pl_mpeg, header-only): `import pl_mpeg;`
  uses MPEG-1 video, MP2 audio and MPEG-PS demuxing from PaskalCPP. A
  self-describing vendor module: it owns every path it needs. The
  implementation is a static library of its own, libpl_mpeg.a (one per
  target, built from its C source by PaskalCPP-Libs' build-pl_mpeg.cmd),
  linked by @linklibrary: every module of the program shares the one copy,
  and a program links only the libraries it imports.

  Open a file with plm_create_with_filename_utf8 (plm_utf8.h, part of the
  package): it takes a UTF-8 path on every target and reads files past
  2 GiB on Windows too, where pl_mpeg's own plm_create_with_filename reads
  the path in the ANSI code page and seeks with a 32-bit offset.

  Read any other source of bytes (an archive entry, an engine's stream) with
  plm_create_with_stream (plm_stream.h, part of the package): two callbacks,
  read and seek, and the data's size; the video ends and loops as a file
  does (pl_mpeg's plm_buffer_create_with_callbacks gives a callback no way to
  say the source has ended).
==============================================================================*/

module unit pl_mpeg;

@addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/pl_mpeg/include";

// The library of each target; Windows needs only mingw's CRT (linked by
// default), Linux also links m.
@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/pl_mpeg/lib/x86_64-windows-gnu";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/pl_mpeg/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu";
  @linklibrary "m";
@else
  @message error "pl_mpeg: unsupported target";
@endif

@linklibrary "pl_mpeg";

// The declarations go to this unit's header, so every importer sees the API
cpp header;

// pl_mpeg.h's declarations use FILE without including stdio.h
#include <stdio.h>
#include <pl_mpeg.h>
#include <plm_utf8.h>
#include <plm_stream.h>

end.
